&lt;p&gt;Reimagine the infrastructure of cancer care within a community that values integrity, inspires growth, and is uniquely positioned to create a more modern, connected oncology ecosystem. We’re looking for an advanced practice provider to help us accomplish our mission to improve and extend lives by learning from the experience of every person with cancer. Are you ready to be the next changemaker in cancer care?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Advanced Practice Provider (APP) on the Clinical Oncology Team, you will use your deep expertise in oncology and genomics to inform the design, development, and optimization of Flatiron Health’s point of care products, tools, and service.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Clinical Oncology Genomics APP will play a critical role as a subject matter expert at the intersection of clinical practice and precision medicine. The role is designed for an advanced practice provider (Nurse Practitioner or Physician Assistant) with deep experience in clinical oncology, genomic testing, somatic and germline test result interpretation, and subsequent patient care and clinical decisions.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Over the term of the contract you will serve as:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clinical-Genomics Product Expert&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the subject matter expert at the intersection of clinical oncology and genomics for Flatiron’s product development teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interpret complex genomic test results and translate clinical workflows into actionable product requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise on the integration of molecular diagnostics and precision medicine into Flatiron’s software solutions, ensuring products reflect real-world clinical needs and best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and validate product features related to genomic data capture, interpretation, and clinical decision support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess the quality of product output to ensure clinical validity and accuracy prior to these features being in the hands of our point of care customers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product &amp;amp; Workflow Enhancement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Product, Engineering, and Clinical teams to inform and test enhancements to clinical workflows in OncoEMR and other Flatiron products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the voice of providers in product discovery, scoping, development, rollout, and maintenance phases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education &amp;amp; Enablement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and deliver educational resources (e.g., guides, presentations, webinars) to help practices utilize point of care genomic testing recommendations, orders, and results in support of personalized patient care.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a resource for Flatiron colleagues, providing clear explanations of genomic concepts and their impact on product design, user experience, and patient impact.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with internal stakeholders to ensure alignment between clinical workflows, product features, and business objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in multidisciplinary discussions focused on the clinical implications of genomics in oncology care.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay current on advances in molecular diagnostics, targeted therapies, and precision medicine guidelines to inform ongoing product innovation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;re a kind, passionate and collaborative problem-solver who values the opportunity to think beyond the way things are.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are an experienced Advanced Practice Provider (NP or PA) with at least 5 years of oncology experience in a community or academic setting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have demonstrated expertise in interpreting somatic genomic test results (e.g., NGS panels) and understand how these results inform treatment decisions and have taken action on them in a clinical setting for patients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You possess a deep understanding of the clinical-genomics landscape, including familiarity with NCCN Guidelines, molecular diagnostics, and precision medicine workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are an excellent communicator who can distill complex genomic concepts for diverse audiences—product managers, engineers, designers, and other non-clinical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are passionate about education and have experience developing or delivering training on clinical-genomics topics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are collaborative, resourceful, and thrive in a fast-paced environment focused on improving cancer care through technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are available for intermittent travel in support of practice engagements and go lives.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are available for a 6-month contract engagement with flexibility to ramp up quickly and deliver impact in a defined timeframe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Extra credit&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with OncoEMR or similar oncology EHRs; experience with Flatiron Assist is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior involvement in clinical research or quality improvement initiatives related to precision medicine.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Certification or advanced training in genomics or precision medicine.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior contract or consulting experience in healthcare technology or product development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Where you’ll work&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this remote position, you have the freedom to choose your preferred work location while aligning your working hours with your team&#39;s. For further details on our hybrid work approach and remote work type, please visit the&lt;a href=&quot;https://flatiron.com/careers/how-we-work?hs_preview=SnRudnya-115772611226&quot;&gt; how we work&lt;/a&gt; website.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Life at Flatiron&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Flatiron Health, we offer a full range of benefits to support you and your loved ones so you can focus your working hours on improving cancer care and accelerating cancer research, and your non-working hours on everything else life has to offer:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work/life autonomy via flexible work hours and flexible paid time off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive compensation package&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) contribution to help you reach your retirement planning goals*&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Financial health resources including 1:1 financial advice&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental well-being tools and services&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Parental benefits and policies including family-building care and generous leave&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Path to parenthood programs supporting fertility, adoption, and surrogacy&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel support for safe healthcare services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*Note: Eligibility for certain benefits may vary for contract employees. Please inquire about specific benefit availability for your contract role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to our robust benefit offerings, visit our Life at Flatiron page to learn how we support continuous learning and celebrate inclusion and belonging in the workplace.&lt;/p&gt;
